"""Advance widths for Inter, the face every launch-reel line is set in.

Everything in a launch reel is centred or wrapped against a measured width: a headline that
rises out of a mask, a pill that resizes to its label, a chat bubble that hugs its question.
A flat per-character guess puts a centred headline visibly off centre, so carry the real table,
measured off the variable Inter the web app ships as "Inter Brand", at the five weights the
scenes use. No kerning: Inter's kerning moves a line by well under 1%, which a mask with 30px
of padding absorbs.
"""
